    description: "`hypergumbo symbols <repo> | head -c 10` exits 1, not 141. Owner ruling 2026-11-19 (WI-nidun): a broken pipe exits 141 for the whole CLI, so 1 always means a violated claim.\n\nREPRO (dev 3c109b3aa): hypergumbo symbols packages/hypergumbo-tracker | head -c 10; echo ${PIPESTATUS[0]} -> 1, nothing on stderr. Control: hypergumbo sketch packages/hypergumbo-tracker | head -c 10 -> 141.\n\nMECHANISM (traced in-process): cmd_symbols (cli.py ~5521) prints through rich.console.Console. On EPIPE, rich calls Console.on_broken_pipe, which redirects stdout to /dev/null and raises SystemExit(1). SystemExit is not an Exception, so main()'s `except BrokenPipeError` (cli.py ~14072) never sees it.\n\nSCOPE: grep of packages/*/src finds two Console( sites: cli.py cmd_symbols (stdout) and sketch.py:286 (stderr=True). Only the stdout one is affected today.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: a Console subclass whose on_broken_pipe sets quiet and re-raises BrokenPipeError, plus a test that drives symbols into a closed pipe and asserts 141; consider a structural guard that every stdout Console is that subclass. cli.py change: ride a PR that already selects most of the suite."  # 8ad9
    fields: {}  # 8ad9
